    "resetMethod": "For each cold-audit comparison, remove only the two directional checkpoint documents on the owned local and remote fixture, retaining the imported bodies and database identities. Run batches in ascending size order; elapsed times are single samples with warmed caches, not medians.",
    "rttInjection": "One artificial RTT per HTTP request: half before forwarding the intact request, half before forwarding response headers. Streaming bytes are not rate limited. Twenty milliseconds is an injected delay, not an Internet measurement.",
    "checkpointComparison": "The local-only checkpoint trial also reduces batches_limit from 25 to two. Request removal is directly observed, but the elapsed-time difference does not isolate checkpoint mode as its sole cause."
  },
  "requestModel": {
    "defaultKnownPush": "Kp = ceil(44000/b). Each non-empty batch sends _revs_diff and remote checkpoint GET then PUT: 3Kp requests and approximately 3Kp sequential RTTs. No bodies are sent when all revisions are known.",
    "defaultKnownPull": "Kl = ceil(4000/b), with the leaf-excluding pull selector. Non-empty batches contribute _changes, asynchronous database info, and remote checkpoint GET then PUT: 4Kl requests. Read-ahead and asynchronous info overlap; this is not 4Kl serial RTTs.",
    "observedTotal": "3Kp + 4Kl + 7 for this fixture. Fixed and terminal overhead depends on setup and scheduling; seven is not a universal constant.",
    "wallTime": "Push and pull overlap. Use the dominant push waiting term 3KpR here, then account for startup, bytes, CPU, storage, and scheduling. Do not multiply total bidirectional requests by RTT.",
    "fastFetch": "Five 10000-row continuous pages plus seven progress/status _changes requests, for twelve requests. This is the stream function only.",
    "localCheckpointTrial": "Kp + 2Kl + 4 = 212 audit requests at b250, followed by eight publication/verification requests at zero injected RTT, including two remote checkpoint PUTs. The leading push wait becomes KpR, plus constant publication and other costs. Full revision comparison is retained.",
    "limitations": "More matching control/tombstone rows, conflicts, missing bodies, concurrent writes, and failures change the work. A high update_seq number is not itself a count of changes-feed rows."
  },
